.TITLE "diff"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Compares two files line by line. It identifies __differences__ between text files and displays the changes required to make them identical.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**diff file1 file2**
Compares two files and displays the lines that differ.
> __file1__ first file | __file2__ second file

**diff -u file1 file2**
Produces a unified diff format which is commonly used for patches.
> __-u__ unified format flag

**diff -i file1 file2**
Ignores case differences when comparing file contents.
> __-i__ ignore case flag

**diff -r folder1 folder2**
Compares the contents of two directories recursively.
> __-r__ recursive flag

**diff -w file1 file2**
Ignores all white space when comparing lines.
> __-w__ ignore white space flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Unified diffs generated with __-u__ are the industry standard for sharing code changes. When comparing large directories, using __-r__ alongside __-q__ can provide a quick summary of which files differ without showing the content changes.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"

documentation: __https://ss64.com/osx/diff.html__
